[ti:Secrecy in Industry]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.37]Lesson 15 | 第15课
[00:02.58]Secrecy in industry | 工业中的秘密
[00:10.68]Why is secrecy particularly important in the chemical industries? | 为什么保密在化学工业中特别重要？
[00:17.82]Two factors weigh heavily against the effectiveness of scientific research in industry. | 有两个因素严重妨碍了工业中科学研究的效力。
[00:25.27]One is the general atmosphere of secrecy in which it is carried out, | 一是普遍的保密气氛，研究就是在这种气氛中进行的，
[00:31.01]the other the lack of freedom of the individual research worker. | 另一个是各个研究工作者缺乏自由。
[00:36.05]In so far as any inquiry is a secret one, | 就任何一项研究属于保密性质而言，
[00:40.13]it naturally limits all those engaged in carrying it out from effective contact with their fellow scientists either in other countries or in universities, | 它自然限制了从事该项研究的人员与国外或大学的同行科学家进行有效接触，
[00:51.21]or even, often enough, in other departments of the same firm. | 甚至常常不能与同一公司其他部门的人员接触。
[00:57.33]The degree of secrecy naturally varies considerably. | 保密的程度自然差别很大。
[01:01.76]Some of the bigger firms are engaged in researches which are of such general and fundamental nature | 某些大公司所从事的研究具有如此普遍和根本的性质，
[01:09.15]that it is a positive advantage to them not to keep them secret. | 以至于不保密反而对它们有绝对的好处。
[01:15.02]Yet a great many processes depending on such research are sought for with complete secrecy until the stage at which patents can be taken out. | 然而许多依赖这种研究的工艺过程，在取得专利之前是处于完全保密状态下探求的。
[01:25.75]Even more processes are never patented at all but kept as secret processes. | 更多的工艺过程根本就不申请专利，而是作为秘密工序保存着。
[01:32.43]This applies particularly to chemical industries, | 这特别适用于化学工业，
[01:37.00]where chance discoveries play a much larger part than they do in physical and mechanical industries. | 因为在化学工业中，偶然的发现所起的作用比在物理和机械工业中所起的作用要大得多。
[01:44.51]Sometimes the secrecy goes to such an extent that the whole nature of the research cannot be mentioned. | 有时保密到了这种地步，连研究的整个性质都不能提及。
[01:53.17]Many firms, for instance have great difficulty in obtaining technical or scientific books from libraries | 例如，许多公司在从图书馆借科技书籍时就遇到很大的困难，
[02:00.95]because they are unwilling to have their names entered as having taken out such and such a book, | 因为他们不愿意让自己的名字被登记为借过某本书，
[02:07.65]for fear the agents of other firms should be able to trace the kind of research they are likely to be undertaking. | 生怕其他公司的情报人员能够查出他们可能正在从事的研究类型。
